ance":0.5352,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"IND","distance":0.5435,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Frank Reich"},{"season":2022,"team":"BUF","distance":0.5552,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"LV","distance":0.5608,"shared":12,"play_caller":null}],"defense":[{"season":2023,"team":"LV","distance":0.4781,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Patrick Graham"},{"season":2023,"team":"BAL","distance":0.4889,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Mike Macdonald"},{"season":2022,"team":"SEA","distance":0.5242,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"NO","distance":0.5299,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dennis Allen"},{"season":2025,"team":"TEN","distance":0.5589,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dennard Wilson"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Texans are 3-6 through week 10 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 233 to 219. The offense ranks 9th in EPA per play and the defense 16th in EPA allowed, so neither side has stood out much yet. The record undersells them so far, since teams with numbers like these usually win more often. What sets them apart is an eight man box rate that was among the highest in the league.","offense":"The Texans offense has been well above average by EPA per play so far, and it has been much better passing the ball than running it. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. C.J. Stroud has run the passing game, with Nico Collins leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Texans defense has been about average by EPA allowed per play so far. Its strongest area has been sack rate, where it ranks 2nd, and its weakest has been takeaways per game, where it ranks 21st. Danielle Hunter has been as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise is Jadeveon Clowney, who has 4.5 sacks while playing only 42% of the snaps, after not being a regular on this defense last season. Schematically, they have an eight man box rate that was among the highest in the league.","special":"The Texans have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 95% of field goals, which is one of the best in the league. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the defensive line, about 32% of the money on the books.","players":"C.J. Stroud has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 2,462 yards. Targets have been spread around, with Nico Collins and Xavier Hutchinson leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. Woody Marks has handled most of the work in the backfield with 55% of the carries. On defense, Will Anderson leads the team with 10.5 sacks and Calen Bullock has picked off 2 passes.","coaching":"Nick Caley is calling the offense and DeMeco Ryans is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2024 Cowboys under Mike McCarthy and the 2024 Browns. Their defense looks most like the 2023 Raiders under Patrick Graham and the 2023 Ravens under Mike Macdonald.","trends":"The offense went from 21st in EPA per play in 2025 to 9th so far this season, a big step forward. The defense moved from 1st in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 16th so far this season, a big step back. The biggest change in approach was two point attempt rate, which went from 17% to 4%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}